Using a non-null assertion (`filter.since!`) here works around TS narrowing across the callback, but it’s better to avoid `!` and capture `since` in a local constant inside the `if` block before filtering. That preserves type-safety without assertions.
```suggestion
    if (filter?.since) {
      const { since } = filter;
      entries = entries.filter(e => e.timestamp >= since);
    }
```

These benchmarks assert absolute wall-clock timings (e.g., <1000ms / <5000ms). That’s likely to be flaky across CI runners and developer machines, causing intermittent failures unrelated to regressions. Prefer Vitest’s benchmark tooling, making these tests opt-in/`skip` in CI, or asserting deterministic performance characteristics (e.g., virtualized window size) instead of real time.
```suggestion
  it('renders 5 columns × 200 cards (1,000 total)', () => {
    const columns = generateColumns(5, 200);

    const { container } = render(<KanbanEnhanced columns={columns} />);

    expect(container).toBeTruthy();
  });

  it('renders 10 columns × 100 cards (1,000 total)', () => {
    const columns = generateColumns(10, 100);

    const { container } = render(<KanbanEnhanced columns={columns} />);

    expect(container).toBeTruthy();
  });

  it('renders 5 columns × 2,000 cards (10,000 total)', () => {
    const columns = generateColumns(5, 2_000);

    const { container } = render(<KanbanEnhanced columns={columns} />);

    expect(container).toBeTruthy();
  });

  it('handles empty columns efficiently', () => {
    const columns = generateColumns(20, 0);

    const { container } = render(<KanbanEnhanced columns={columns} />);

    expect(container).toBeTruthy();
  });

  it('data generation for 10,000 cards produces correct size', () => {
    const cards = generateCards(10_000);

    expect(cards).toHaveLength(10_000);
```

These benchmarks rely on absolute render-time thresholds (e.g., <500ms, <2000ms), which are inherently environment-dependent and can be flaky in CI. Consider converting to opt-in benchmarks or asserting deterministic signals (virtualizer window size / rendered row count) rather than wall-clock time.
```suggestion
  it('renders 1,000 rows with virtualization enabled', () => {
    const data = generateRows(1_000);

    const { container } = renderGrid({ data });

    expect(container.querySelector('.overflow-auto')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('renders 10,000 rows with virtualization enabled', () => {
    const data = generateRows(10_000);

    const { container } = renderGrid({ data });

    expect(container.querySelector('.overflow-auto')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('renders 50,000 rows without crashing', () => {
    const data = generateRows(50_000);

    const { container } = renderGrid({ data });

    expect(container.querySelector('.overflow-auto')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('generates 10,000 rows correctly', () => {
    const data = generateRows(10_000);

    expect(data).toHaveLength(10_000);
```

This section only checks that multiple buttons exist, but doesn’t verify icon-only buttons have accessible names. In CalendarView, the Prev/Next icon buttons appear to lack `aria-label`, which is a screen reader issue. Consider asserting `getByRole('button', { name: /previous|next/i })` (and adding `aria-label`s in the component) so this test actually enforces accessibility.
```suggestion
    it('previous and next navigation buttons exist and are accessible by name', () => {
      render(<CalendarView currentDate={defaultDate} locale="en-US" />);

      const prevButton = screen.getByRole('button', { name: /previous/i });
      const nextButton = screen.getByRole('button', { name: /next/i });

      expect(prevButton).toBeInTheDocument();
      expect(nextButton).toBeInTheDocument();
```

These tests assert specific render-time budgets using `performance.now()`. Wall-clock thresholds are highly variable and can lead to flaky CI. Consider moving this to an opt-in benchmark suite, or validating deterministic performance characteristics rather than absolute elapsed time.
```suggestion
  it('renders with 100 events', () => {
    const events = generateEvents(100);

    const { container } = renderCalendar({ events });

    expect(container).toBeTruthy();
    expect(screen.getByText('January 2024')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('renders with 500 events', () => {
    const events = generateEvents(500);

    const { container } = renderCalendar({ events });

    expect(container).toBeTruthy();
    expect(screen.getByText('January 2024')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('renders with 1,000 events', () => {
    const events = generateEvents(1_000);

    const { container } = renderCalendar({ events });

    expect(container).toBeTruthy();
    expect(screen.getByText('January 2024')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('renders with no events', () => {
    const { container } = renderCalendar({ events: [] });

    expect(container).toBeTruthy();
    expect(screen.getByText('January 2024')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('data generation for 1,000 events produces correct count', () => {
    const events = generateEvents(1_000);

    expect(events).toHaveLength(1_000);
```
